  "name": "CREATININE & EGFR (CT)",
  "code": "1070",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"159\" data-end=\"212\">This test evaluates <strong data-start=\"179\" data-end=\"198\">kidney function</strong> by measuring:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"214\" data-end=\"473\">\n<li data-start=\"214\" data-end=\"302\">\n<p data-start=\"216\" data-end=\"302\"><strong data-start=\"216\" data-end=\"236\">Serum Creatinine</strong>: A waste product from muscle metabolism, filtered by the kidneys.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"303\" data-end=\"473\">\n<p data-start=\"305\" data-end=\"473\"><strong data-start=\"305\" data-end=\"352\">eGFR (estimated Glomerular Filtration Rate)</strong>: A calculated value using serum creatinine, age, sex, and sometimes race to estimate how well the kidneys are filtering.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"475\" data-end=\"498\">It is commonly used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"500\" data-end=\"658\">\n<li data-start=\"500\" data-end=\"545\">\n<p data-start=\"502\" data-end=\"545\">Screen for <strong data-start=\"513\" data-end=\"545\">chronic kidney disease (CKD)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"546\" data-end=\"591\">\n<p data-start=\"548\" data-end=\"591\">Monitor progression of <strong data-start=\"571\" data-end=\"591\">renal impairment</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"592\" data-end=\"658\">\n<p data-start=\"594\" data-end=\"658\">Guide medication dosing in patients with reduced kidney function</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start=\"717\" data-end=\"745\"><strong data-start=\"722\" data-end=\"745\">Elevated Creatinine</strong></h4>\n<p data-start=\"746\" data-end=\"845\">High serum creatinine suggests <strong data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"805\">impaired kidney function</strong> or <strong data-start=\"809\" data-end=\"844\">decreased glomerular filtration</strong>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Possible Causes</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Explanation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Chronic kidney disease (CKD)</strong></td>\n<td>Progressive loss of kidney function over months/years</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Acute kidney injury (AKI)</strong></td>\n<td>Sudden decline in renal function due to dehydration, toxins, or obstruction</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Severe dehydration</strong></td>\n<td>Reduces renal perfusion, leading to increased creatinine</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Urinary tract obstruction</strong></td>\n<td>Causes backpressure and decreased filtration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>High muscle mass or intense exercise</strong></td>\n<td>May mildly raise creatinine without disease</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"746\" data-end=\"845\">&nbsp;</p>",
